insert into public.ai_playbook(version,content) select 16, content || '

## Paperwork loop: tree, request and files must agree (Alexander, November 6, 2026)
Goal: get every correct document in as fast as possible so the file can be completed. Do these on EVERY review once a family tree or document request exists:
1. Does the family tree make sense? Check it against the deed owners, death certificates, wills, obituaries, the seller''s emails and staff notes: every deed owner appears; living/deceased matches the evidence; spouses, children and heirs are plausible (ages, surnames after marriage, dates of death in order); nobody is duplicated under two spellings; the signer is someone the rules allow to sign. Write down each thing that does not add up.
2. When it is wrong and the evidence clearly shows the right answer, propose edit_family_tree with the corrected tree now (quote the evidence in reason), then sync_checklist if needed.
3. When it is wrong or unclear and the file does NOT settle it, propose a reply_email asking the seller short, specific clarifying questions (numbered, plain words, e.g. "Did your father remarry after your mother passed?", "Does your brother John have any children?"). Ask only what changes who signs or which documents are needed. Never guess a relative into or out of the tree.
4. When the seller''s answer to those questions is in the thread, take it: propose edit_family_tree with the fix, then send_document_request so the seller receives the corrected request (with the verified plot wording and rebuilt POAs/affidavits). Tell them briefly in the request what changed and that anything already sent still counts where it still applies.
5. Is the request right for the tree? Compare DOCUMENT REQUEST ITEMS with what the corrected tree requires: missing items, items for the wrong person, items no longer needed. Fix via the tree (edit_family_tree / sync_checklist); use edit_document_request only for changes the tree cannot express.
6. Match files to items. For every file on record (uploads, email attachments, profile and document files), read it and decide which item it really is and for which person. Use update_document_items to attach each correct file to its item, and to remove/detach files wrongly attached to an item (wrong person, wrong document type, unreadable, wrong cemetery/plot) with a short note why. A photo or scan never marks a needs-notary original received — attach it and leave the state.
7. Then tell the seller in one clear reply exactly what is still missing, per person, so nothing goes back and forth twice.
' from public.ai_playbook where version=15 and deleted_at is null and not exists (select 1 from public.ai_playbook where version=16);
